            <div xml:id="d365">

                <pb facs="0567" n="443" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg443"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/2732: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morales</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-10-30T13:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 30,
                                1923—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 31—8:55
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>90. Referring to the Legation’s telegram of October 30, 8 a.m.<anchor n="14"
                        xml:id="d365-f1"/> The polls at Tegucigalpa reopened yesterday morning and
                    no disorders reported throughout the Republic. The final vote as given by the
                    Government, with the exception of a few towns which will not materially affect
                    the count, is as follows: Carias 46,800, Bonilla 33,000, and Arias 18,000. …</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morales</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
